WEBVTT


00:00:53.627 --> 00:01:00.817
EXTRATERRESTRIAL


00:03:06.107 --> 00:03:07.699
-Don't shout.
-Don't shout.


00:03:07.907 --> 00:03:09.306
Sorry, sorry.


00:03:20.307 --> 00:03:22.696
-I'll get dressed, okay?
-Okay.


00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:32.216
Hey...


00:03:32.427 --> 00:03:33.542
What?


00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:37.906
Do you know where my pants are?


00:03:38.107 --> 00:03:39.699
In the living room.


00:03:59.987 --> 00:04:01.579
NO SIGNAL


00:04:10.827 --> 00:04:13.387
Last night everything
fell out of my pocket


00:04:13.547 --> 00:04:16.425
and I'm missing a two euro coin.


00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:30.296
It's only two euros.
You can pay next time.


00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:31.900
Don't worry about it.


00:04:32.107 --> 00:04:33.017
Here.


00:04:43.427 --> 00:04:44.701
Anyway...


00:04:44.907 --> 00:04:46.465
Can I have some coffee?


00:04:53.187 --> 00:04:54.745
It's burning.


00:05:08.427 --> 00:05:09.143
Thanks.


00:05:09.307 --> 00:05:10.217
You're welcome.


00:05:11.987 --> 00:05:14.865
I'm sorry but something urgent
came up...


00:05:20.747 --> 00:05:22.658
Do you mind if I make a call?


00:05:22.867 --> 00:05:26.906
There's something wrong with my cell,
there's no coverage.


00:05:36.867 --> 00:05:38.585
This isn't working either.


00:05:38.787 --> 00:05:39.776
Hold on.


00:05:45.347 --> 00:05:47.622
Mine has no coverage either.


00:05:48.947 --> 00:05:51.302
What time does yours say?


00:05:51.467 --> 00:05:54.061
-Just past 7:30.
-Just past 7:30?


00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:56.622
Yeah, the day got away from us.


00:05:56.827 --> 00:06:00.342
Listen, I really need to be alone.
I'm sorry.


00:06:00.507 --> 00:06:04.056
No one around, at this time?
Even on a Sunday...


00:06:36.067 --> 00:06:38.786
Has something happened?
Did you hear anything?


00:06:52.827 --> 00:06:54.738
None of the channels are working.


00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:57.302
It's been like that since I got up.


00:06:57.627 --> 00:06:59.504
What about the internet?


00:07:04.067 --> 00:07:05.625
...in a state of emergency.


00:07:05.827 --> 00:07:09.024
Please stay calm
and remain in your homes


00:07:09.187 --> 00:07:12.338
until emergency crews arrive.


00:07:12.507 --> 00:07:16.500
Contact them and follow
their instructions. Thank you.


00:07:17.107 --> 00:07:20.258
Holy shit! What is that?


00:07:20.827 --> 00:07:22.704
A temporary evacuation is underway...


00:07:22.907 --> 00:07:24.022
There, out back.


00:07:26.627 --> 00:07:29.221
-Got any binoculars?
-No.


00:07:29.347 --> 00:07:31.622
...until emergency crews arrive.


00:07:31.827 --> 00:07:33.260
The camera...


00:07:36.187 --> 00:07:38.860
This is a message
from the Department of Defense.


00:07:39.067 --> 00:07:40.944
-This is the zoom, right?
-Yeah.


00:08:09.027 --> 00:08:10.426
How big is it?


00:08:13.827 --> 00:08:16.625
Look, it's turning very slowly.


00:08:18.267 --> 00:08:19.063
Yeah.


00:08:19.267 --> 00:08:23.897
I think I can figure it out.
If I time how long it takes to turn


00:08:24.707 --> 00:08:27.744
I can work out its size.
Got a calculator?


00:08:27.907 --> 00:08:29.306
Yeah, you want it?


00:08:29.547 --> 00:08:30.662
Yes, please.


00:08:33.747 --> 00:08:35.226
Hey, excuse me...


00:08:35.347 --> 00:08:36.985
-Julio.
-Oh, I'm Julia.


00:08:37.987 --> 00:08:39.898
What a coincidence.


00:08:40.307 --> 00:08:43.185
I don't know why I thought
your name was Luisa.


00:08:43.547 --> 00:08:46.744
After last night no wonder
I can't remember...


00:08:47.067 --> 00:08:49.422
By the way, where did we meet?


00:08:50.347 --> 00:08:53.225
Hey, aren't you worried
about anybody?


00:08:53.707 --> 00:08:57.700
I guess I should call my family,
they're all in Badajoz.


00:08:58.227 --> 00:09:00.422
If the phones are working later.


00:09:00.627 --> 00:09:02.857
You must have somewhere to go.


00:09:04.947 --> 00:09:05.936
Yeah.


00:09:06.467 --> 00:09:08.105
Yeah, my apartment.


00:09:08.267 --> 00:09:10.178
I live in Hortaleza.


00:09:10.347 --> 00:09:14.181
I'm renting a room
from some friends of my parents.


00:09:22.307 --> 00:09:24.218
I can leave if you want.


00:09:24.987 --> 00:09:27.899
No, wait till I find the calculator.


00:09:28.107 --> 00:09:29.381
Should I leave after that?


00:09:29.547 --> 00:09:30.696
No...


00:09:33.107 --> 00:09:35.462
Sorry, what was the calculator
for again?


00:09:55.067 --> 00:09:56.819
There's somebody there.


00:10:04.347 --> 00:10:05.257
Hi.


00:10:07.267 --> 00:10:08.746
-Angel.
-Hi.


00:10:11.627 --> 00:10:14.346
This is...
What was your name again?


00:10:15.427 --> 00:10:16.576
Julio.


00:10:17.107 --> 00:10:19.496
I'm Julia, what a coincidence.


00:10:21.267 --> 00:10:22.859
He's a friend...


00:10:23.707 --> 00:10:25.584
I think you were right
to stay home.


00:10:25.787 --> 00:10:28.176
People were so quick to take off.


00:10:28.307 --> 00:10:30.741
Where could be better than right here?


00:10:31.627 --> 00:10:32.776
Wow.


00:10:36.347 --> 00:10:38.338
Is there anyone else
left in the building?


00:10:38.507 --> 00:10:40.099
Actually, I don't know.


00:10:40.267 --> 00:10:45.102
Trucks showed up around nine
with the military and they organized


00:10:45.267 --> 00:10:47.462
the cars into lines.
I think everyone left but...


00:10:49.027 --> 00:10:51.541
I don't really know
because I didn't open the door.


00:10:51.747 --> 00:10:54.466
I watched TV all day
until it stopped working.


00:10:54.667 --> 00:10:55.702
Is your internet working?


00:10:56.267 --> 00:10:59.623
What have you been doing all day?
Didn't you hear me ringing?


00:10:59.827 --> 00:11:01.499
Where did they take everyone?


00:11:02.347 --> 00:11:04.907
I don't know, the suburbs,
the mountains...


00:11:05.107 --> 00:11:08.622
Not far, because
there are more there.


00:11:09.547 --> 00:11:10.662
More what?


00:11:12.107 --> 00:11:14.541
More ships.
Don't you know what's going on?


00:11:14.747 --> 00:11:16.465
Angel, is your internet working?


00:11:16.667 --> 00:11:18.578
Worldwide they don't know,


00:11:18.787 --> 00:11:22.143
but in Spain
more than 30 have appeared.


00:11:22.267 --> 00:11:24.258
Especially over the cities.


00:11:26.467 --> 00:11:30.062
Have you been in bed all day?
I tried ringing the bell...


00:11:30.267 --> 00:11:32.462
How did you know she was here?


00:11:32.867 --> 00:11:33.856
What?


00:11:34.027 --> 00:11:37.099
Why didn't you think
she'd left with the others?


00:11:40.147 --> 00:11:42.661
Because Julia always parks her car
in front of mine.


00:11:42.867 --> 00:11:45.335
And it was there this morning,
that's how.


00:11:45.507 --> 00:11:49.056
But you said you didn't go outside.
How did you see it?


00:11:49.267 --> 00:11:50.495
From the window?


00:11:51.947 --> 00:11:52.697
Yes.


00:11:54.867 --> 00:11:55.617
No.


00:11:57.227 --> 00:11:58.785
My internet isn't working.


00:11:59.067 --> 00:12:00.182
No...


00:12:02.667 --> 00:12:03.816
Anyway...


00:12:04.667 --> 00:12:05.782
I'm going...


00:12:05.947 --> 00:12:07.096
to the bathroom.


00:12:07.267 --> 00:12:09.019
No, I'm leaving.


00:12:10.267 --> 00:12:12.497
I'll call you later, Julia.


00:12:31.547 --> 00:12:33.424
I think it's almost...


00:12:36.307 --> 00:12:38.218
four miles wide.


00:12:38.947 --> 00:12:42.178
Nobody's seen anything coming out,
right?


00:12:42.347 --> 00:12:43.177
Well,


00:12:43.347 --> 00:12:47.943
I think they come down from the middle.
That's why we can't see them from here.


00:12:52.507 --> 00:12:56.022
What's up with your neighbor?
Is he always so transparent?


00:12:58.227 --> 00:12:59.296
What?


00:12:59.627 --> 00:13:02.300
It's obvious he stayed
because he saw your car


00:13:02.467 --> 00:13:04.697
and knew you hadn't left, right?


00:13:05.627 --> 00:13:08.346
How do you know
about all this stuff?


00:13:09.507 --> 00:13:11.384
I'm an industrial designer.


00:13:11.627 --> 00:13:13.857
Actually, I haven't finished my degree,


00:13:14.027 --> 00:13:17.224
but I work making signs,
drawings, models...


00:13:17.347 --> 00:13:19.781
I'm working on something amazing.


00:13:20.667 --> 00:13:24.216
Some friends of my parents...
Well, the ones I'm renting from...


00:13:24.347 --> 00:13:27.862
They're going to be in a parade
in their neighborhood


00:13:28.067 --> 00:13:30.262
and they asked me to make this.


00:13:33.067 --> 00:13:35.979
It's a float, something like this.


00:13:37.387 --> 00:13:39.947
Well, more or less, okay?


00:13:40.867 --> 00:13:44.337
And they want a car to pull the float,


00:13:44.507 --> 00:13:47.783
but what I did was put the car


00:13:47.987 --> 00:13:50.217
inside it.


00:13:53.307 --> 00:13:55.696
Sorry, I'm really tired.


00:13:56.027 --> 00:13:57.619
I'm going to bed.


00:14:01.387 --> 00:14:02.661
See you tomorrow.


00:15:13.467 --> 00:15:14.900
It's okay, it's me.


00:15:15.107 --> 00:15:18.577
-What's wrong? What time is it?
-It's late, almost morning.


00:15:19.307 --> 00:15:22.697
I was looking at the ship


00:15:22.907 --> 00:15:26.536
and I thought, shit.
Anything can happen anytime.


00:15:27.147 --> 00:15:28.136
Yeah.


00:15:28.267 --> 00:15:31.782
I thought we could take turns
keeping watch.


00:15:31.987 --> 00:15:34.820
Don't worry, I'll go first, okay?


00:15:36.027 --> 00:15:37.585
But what happened?


00:15:38.347 --> 00:15:40.781
No, it's just in case.


00:15:40.987 --> 00:15:43.342
I'll wake you up
if something happens, okay?


00:15:46.907 --> 00:15:49.785
-Where are you going?
-The living room, stay there.


00:15:49.987 --> 00:15:52.217
No, I'm not sleepy.


00:15:59.707 --> 00:16:01.982
-Quick, get up.
-What's going on?


00:16:02.867 --> 00:16:05.256
-Are they attacking?
-Get washed.


00:16:15.147 --> 00:16:16.262
Carlos!


00:16:16.787 --> 00:16:17.776
Julia.


00:16:18.027 --> 00:16:19.619
Where have you been?


00:16:19.987 --> 00:16:22.501
They were taking people
to El Escorial...


00:16:22.707 --> 00:16:24.982
Sweetheart, I'm so glad you're here.


00:16:25.307 --> 00:16:28.822
They were taking people to El Escorial
and you weren't there...


00:16:30.907 --> 00:16:33.137
but there were people
from this neighborhood.


00:16:33.267 --> 00:16:37.340
I called and you didn't answer.
And since you had gone out...


00:16:37.907 --> 00:16:40.626
By the way, I'm not alone.


00:16:49.267 --> 00:16:50.256
Hi.


00:16:50.947 --> 00:16:52.505
Carlos, this is...


00:16:52.787 --> 00:16:54.539
-Sorry, what was your name?
-Julio.


00:16:55.027 --> 00:16:57.257
What a coincidence!
Like me.


00:16:57.427 --> 00:16:58.860
-Hi, Julio.
-Hi.


00:16:59.027 --> 00:17:00.255
Feeling any better?


00:17:00.467 --> 00:17:01.263
Yeah.


00:17:01.427 --> 00:17:02.746
You're lucky Julia saw you


00:17:02.907 --> 00:17:07.025
from the window. If you'd blacked out
one street up nobody'd have seen you.


00:17:07.347 --> 00:17:10.066
-I almost did last night.
-What happened?


00:17:10.547 --> 00:17:13.584
I walked here from El Escorial.
Eight and a half hours.


00:17:13.747 --> 00:17:15.578
It got dark at Ciudad Universitaria.


00:17:15.787 --> 00:17:17.618
I spent the night in a tent


00:17:17.827 --> 00:17:21.820
until some jerks woke me up
screaming like crazy all night


00:17:21.987 --> 00:17:23.466
and breaking windows.
Nothing happened


00:17:23.667 --> 00:17:25.419
but it was scary.


00:17:27.307 --> 00:17:29.298
What's this?
Did you draw it?


00:17:29.427 --> 00:17:31.304
Yeah, I'm a designer.


00:17:34.587 --> 00:17:36.020
Have a seat.


00:17:40.027 --> 00:17:41.938
Julio was drawing
what he saw outside for me.


00:17:42.147 --> 00:17:45.617
It's good. Damn, it's spot on.
I know people who've seen it


00:17:45.827 --> 00:17:48.580
closer up and showed me photos
but you can't see shit.


00:17:50.027 --> 00:17:51.176
What's that?


00:17:51.947 --> 00:17:53.346
Holy shit!


00:17:54.787 --> 00:17:57.460
I heard about a weird car
driving around.


00:17:57.667 --> 00:17:58.543
It sounded like


00:17:58.747 --> 00:18:01.819
a military vehicle,
but this is something else.


00:18:02.347 --> 00:18:04.099
This is serious, damn it!


00:18:09.467 --> 00:18:10.616
Where did you see it?


00:18:14.347 --> 00:18:15.462
Out there.


00:18:17.267 --> 00:18:19.064
Here? On this street?


00:18:22.107 --> 00:18:23.586
I didn't see anything.
This is...


00:18:23.787 --> 00:18:24.583
I saw it.


00:18:24.787 --> 00:18:26.106
It drove right past.


00:18:26.307 --> 00:18:28.662
I described it
and this looks a lot like it.


00:18:31.627 --> 00:18:32.776
Nice going, Julio.


00:18:34.947 --> 00:18:36.539
-Good work.
-Thanks.


00:18:41.947 --> 00:18:45.462
-Shit, you could have told me...
-I know, I'm sorry.


00:18:45.667 --> 00:18:48.135
I'd have left right away
and saved you the trouble.


00:18:51.027 --> 00:18:52.619
I put my foot in it.


00:18:53.827 --> 00:18:56.261
I don't know what to say.
I'm sorry.


00:18:59.587 --> 00:19:01.020
What are you doing?


00:19:01.187 --> 00:19:02.302
I'm leaving.


00:19:02.907 --> 00:19:04.056
You're leaving?


00:19:04.267 --> 00:19:05.302
I'm in the way.


00:19:05.467 --> 00:19:07.583
No, you're not.
With all the mayhem out there...


00:19:07.747 --> 00:19:09.544
You might black out again.
Come inside.


00:19:15.747 --> 00:19:17.578
Angel stayed behind too.


00:19:17.867 --> 00:19:19.016
You don't say.


00:19:19.187 --> 00:19:23.100
We can't get rid of that guy,
not even with UFOs. Come in.


00:19:26.747 --> 00:19:29.978
Hi, Angel.
Come by for dinner later!


00:19:40.027 --> 00:19:43.258
The military has fenced off the area
right under the ship.


00:19:43.427 --> 00:19:46.658
Apparently people have seen
some crazy stuff out there.


00:19:47.427 --> 00:19:48.576
Anyway,


00:19:49.307 --> 00:19:52.504
besides that weird tank Julia saw
I don't believe any of it.


00:19:52.667 --> 00:19:54.259
You saw a weird tank?


00:19:54.427 --> 00:19:56.861
Yeah, I have a drawing of it
in there.


00:20:01.027 --> 00:20:05.225
If they brought huge ships all this way
there must be a reason, right?


00:20:05.387 --> 00:20:06.456
They'll do something.


00:20:06.827 --> 00:20:07.896
Maybe...


00:20:08.787 --> 00:20:11.347
Look, I don't mean to scare you,


00:20:11.547 --> 00:20:16.143
but I overheard two cops talking
at a highway checkpoint


00:20:16.467 --> 00:20:19.186
and it's been on my mind
ever since.


00:20:19.947 --> 00:20:22.302
Maybe they're already doing something


00:20:22.507 --> 00:20:25.180
but in a way that we don't realize.


00:20:25.347 --> 00:20:26.097
I think...


00:20:26.307 --> 00:20:27.865
Maybe they're invisible.


00:20:28.027 --> 00:20:31.542
Maybe they can fit in among us
without us noticing.


00:20:31.947 --> 00:20:34.063
But shouldn't we leave?


00:20:34.267 --> 00:20:36.303
There are ships everywhere.


00:20:37.307 --> 00:20:38.137
I think...


00:20:38.307 --> 00:20:41.299
At least we're someplace
we can control.


00:20:46.347 --> 00:20:48.736
Well, I think that's pretty lame.


00:20:48.907 --> 00:20:51.944
They come here in flying devices
bigger than towns


00:20:52.107 --> 00:20:55.019
and suddenly they're worried about
being noticed? It makes no sense.


00:20:55.507 --> 00:20:56.781
What do you think then?


00:20:56.947 --> 00:20:58.062
Let's hear it.


00:20:59.107 --> 00:21:01.143
I think they're testing humans


00:21:01.307 --> 00:21:05.186
to see what we're like,
how we react,


00:21:05.707 --> 00:21:07.140
if we're intelligent,


00:21:07.307 --> 00:21:09.184
if we're brave...
They're probably


00:21:09.347 --> 00:21:11.781
watching us and all the people fleeing
are making fools of themselves


00:21:11.947 --> 00:21:14.541
because there's no need.
I'll pass.


00:21:14.747 --> 00:21:18.581
Then those of us staying home
are doing the right thing.


00:21:20.587 --> 00:21:22.305
We'll get a prize.


00:21:22.747 --> 00:21:24.305
You'll get a prize.


00:21:24.507 --> 00:21:26.418
Carlos, help me with this.


00:21:27.147 --> 00:21:29.297
-No, they're here to stalk us.
-I hope not.


00:21:29.507 --> 00:21:31.498
Because our neighbor
has that covered.


00:21:31.667 --> 00:21:33.658
-Carlos.
-I'm coming.


00:21:37.747 --> 00:21:40.466
Get the peaches I brought,
they're tasty.


00:21:40.667 --> 00:21:42.658
I put them in the fridge.


00:22:01.947 --> 00:22:02.857
What?


00:22:03.987 --> 00:22:04.897
What?


00:22:05.107 --> 00:22:06.381
What's the problem?


00:22:07.067 --> 00:22:08.500
What do you mean?


00:22:08.907 --> 00:22:10.943
No, what's wrong with you?


00:22:11.107 --> 00:22:12.460
Nothing's wrong with me.


00:22:12.667 --> 00:22:14.305
What's with that face?


00:22:14.587 --> 00:22:17.181
What's with what face?


00:22:18.667 --> 00:22:20.305
Come on, I can tell.


00:22:20.507 --> 00:22:21.986
You can tell what?


00:22:22.907 --> 00:22:24.181
That you're jealous.


00:22:24.747 --> 00:22:26.066
Jealous of what?


00:22:30.387 --> 00:22:31.979
You can tell I'm jealous of what?


00:22:33.187 --> 00:22:36.577
That you're into her
and you haven't screwed her.


00:22:36.787 --> 00:22:37.936
Oh, yeah?


00:22:39.907 --> 00:22:42.262
And why should I be jealous?


00:22:42.947 --> 00:22:46.098
You know exactly why.
You must have heard us fucking


00:22:46.307 --> 00:22:47.706
or something.


00:22:50.307 --> 00:22:53.140
Don't give me that look
like you didn't know.


00:22:55.907 --> 00:22:58.137
You knew, stop pretending.


00:22:59.947 --> 00:23:01.266
You didn't know?


00:23:08.307 --> 00:23:09.376
Try to open this.


00:23:09.547 --> 00:23:10.775
My hands are wet.


00:23:12.547 --> 00:23:14.822
Let me see if I can...


00:23:15.867 --> 00:23:19.064
We're short on food.
We can check


00:23:19.267 --> 00:23:21.622
the neighbors' apartments.
I think the supermarket


00:23:21.787 --> 00:23:23.379
out back stayed open.


00:23:23.827 --> 00:23:27.342
In the worst case we can plant
something on the terrace.


00:23:28.547 --> 00:23:29.377
What do you think, Angel?


00:23:30.467 --> 00:23:31.582
Should we plant lettuce?


00:23:31.747 --> 00:23:34.215
Maybe the spacemen
will give us diplomas.


00:23:36.747 --> 00:23:37.497
Carlos...


00:23:38.347 --> 00:23:39.257
Shit!


00:23:40.307 --> 00:23:41.296
Damn.


00:23:41.787 --> 00:23:43.505
-It's nothing.
-Are you sure?


00:23:43.707 --> 00:23:45.186
Damn it!


00:24:01.107 --> 00:24:02.699
I'm really sorry.
Does it hurt?


00:24:02.907 --> 00:24:06.786
Next time aim the other way
and hold it tighter.


00:24:07.467 --> 00:24:09.105
I can't stand that guy.


00:24:09.307 --> 00:24:13.095
Sometimes I wish he'd fuck her to see
if he'd calm down and leave us alone.


00:24:13.307 --> 00:24:14.376
Julia?


00:24:14.547 --> 00:24:17.380
Hard to believe I thought
he was a snooty homo at first.


00:24:17.587 --> 00:24:19.862
But you can totally tell
he's into Julia.


00:24:20.027 --> 00:24:21.904
You can tell, you can tell...


00:24:22.187 --> 00:24:25.020
Angel, nothing happened!
Don't make things up!


00:24:25.267 --> 00:24:27.019
Nothing happened!


00:24:33.387 --> 00:24:35.821
Thanks for dinner.
See you tomorrow.


00:24:38.787 --> 00:24:41.017
I'm going to bed too.


00:24:55.347 --> 00:24:56.462
Wake up!


00:25:00.707 --> 00:25:02.026
Is it my turn?


00:25:02.387 --> 00:25:04.025
No more turns. You're leaving.


00:25:04.187 --> 00:25:05.745
Leaving? Why am I leaving?


00:25:06.907 --> 00:25:10.422
How could you tell Angel that?
How dare you!


00:25:15.507 --> 00:25:16.940
What did I tell him?


00:25:17.747 --> 00:25:20.307
You know exactly what you told him.


00:25:20.507 --> 00:25:21.781
No, I don't.


00:25:21.947 --> 00:25:24.984
You and I never had sex, okay?


00:25:25.147 --> 00:25:27.820
I know we didn't.
What are you talking about?


00:25:28.187 --> 00:25:29.461
Hypocrite.


00:25:29.667 --> 00:25:33.455
You're lecturing me on sincerity?
You of all people.


00:25:35.867 --> 00:25:38.256
Where will I go?
It's cold.


00:25:39.387 --> 00:25:41.617
Let me eat something first,
I'm hungry.


00:25:41.787 --> 00:25:42.697
Here.


00:25:44.587 --> 00:25:46.817
Really, Julia, I didn't say anything.


00:25:46.987 --> 00:25:49.820
Maybe I said something
and he understood whatever he wanted.


00:25:50.027 --> 00:25:51.426
Who cares anyway?


00:25:51.627 --> 00:25:54.187
You don't know him.
He's lost his mind.


00:25:54.347 --> 00:25:56.258
Well, he'll get over it.


00:25:57.547 --> 00:26:01.335
Last night he said
if I don't tell him, he will.


00:26:01.547 --> 00:26:02.662
Shit.


00:26:03.667 --> 00:26:05.578
Come to my place if you want.


00:26:06.907 --> 00:26:07.896
Wait, wait!


00:26:08.067 --> 00:26:09.978
Just one thing and I'll leave.


00:26:10.187 --> 00:26:11.336
But please, listen to me.


00:26:30.627 --> 00:26:33.061
You win, asshole!


00:29:15.707 --> 00:29:16.617
Julio...


00:29:16.827 --> 00:29:18.704
I went to the supermarket.


00:29:19.467 --> 00:29:21.856
The one you said.


00:29:22.187 --> 00:29:24.098
Why did you go by yourself?


00:29:24.307 --> 00:29:25.456
Come in.


00:29:42.867 --> 00:29:45.142
What the fuck are you doing?


00:29:45.307 --> 00:29:46.899
-It doesn't fit.
-What doesn't?


00:29:47.067 --> 00:29:49.900
Angel. He said he never left
his apartment,


00:29:50.107 --> 00:29:53.179
but he knew your car was parked
in front of his, right?


00:29:53.347 --> 00:29:54.462
Yeah, so what?


00:29:54.627 --> 00:29:58.142
It turns out his car
is the one that isn't there.


00:29:58.307 --> 00:29:59.899
You mean it was stolen?


00:30:00.067 --> 00:30:02.456
Who'd steal that crate?
At least parked next to yours...


00:30:02.667 --> 00:30:06.706
What are the chances everybody
would leave the building except him?


00:30:06.867 --> 00:30:10.382
Telling us some crazy story
and watching us the whole time...


00:30:11.147 --> 00:30:14.025
And the strangest thing...


00:30:15.267 --> 00:30:17.178
What scares me the most...


00:30:18.907 --> 00:30:20.022
What?


00:30:20.787 --> 00:30:24.780
I swear to God I didn't tell him
anything about us.


00:30:26.467 --> 00:30:27.616
What do you mean?


00:30:27.787 --> 00:30:31.177
There's something strange about Angel,
we can't trust him


00:30:31.347 --> 00:30:34.066
and I think Carlos should know
right away.


00:30:34.267 --> 00:30:37.418
Julio! You didn't bring
an extension lead, did you?


00:30:38.467 --> 00:30:39.786
What?


00:30:46.187 --> 00:30:49.259
Did you see how he reacted
to what you said last night?


00:30:49.427 --> 00:30:53.466
About them being among us?
He freaked out.


00:30:55.467 --> 00:30:59.460
Okay, are you guys telling me
there's a chance


00:30:59.627 --> 00:31:03.666
the Angel next door
isn't the Angel we know?


00:31:06.067 --> 00:31:07.625
I don't know him at all,


00:31:07.827 --> 00:31:11.342
but he seems very weird to me,
a troublemaker.


00:31:11.547 --> 00:31:13.185
I don't know about you guys...


00:31:15.387 --> 00:31:16.979
What did he say to you last night?


00:31:17.787 --> 00:31:19.061
At dinner,


00:31:19.267 --> 00:31:20.859
when you two were alone.


00:31:21.067 --> 00:31:23.262
Before he took off all of a sudden.


00:31:23.827 --> 00:31:27.820
He said something to you.
It's been troubling you ever since.


00:31:32.787 --> 00:31:34.857
That you've been acting strangely.


00:31:37.787 --> 00:31:40.017
That there's something odd
about you.


00:31:40.907 --> 00:31:43.467
I said I didn't believe him,
of course.


00:31:43.747 --> 00:31:46.136
That's why he took off like that.


00:31:51.747 --> 00:31:55.137
Look, it's unlikely this Angel
is not the real Angel...


00:32:01.147 --> 00:32:03.502
but we can't take any chances.


00:32:12.267 --> 00:32:13.825
Hey, what's up?


00:32:13.987 --> 00:32:14.976
Hi.


00:32:20.747 --> 00:32:23.580
Did you take the peaches
with you last night?


00:32:23.787 --> 00:32:25.903
No, I left them here.


00:32:26.067 --> 00:32:28.137
I don't see them anywhere.


00:32:29.827 --> 00:32:31.579
I didn't take them.


00:32:31.787 --> 00:32:33.220
-Hi.
-Hi.


00:32:34.347 --> 00:32:36.622
Are you calling me a liar?


00:32:37.067 --> 00:32:38.182
What?


00:32:38.627 --> 00:32:40.857
Are you calling me a liar?


00:32:41.907 --> 00:32:43.818
Why would you lie to me?


00:32:44.027 --> 00:32:45.938
I don't know, you tell me.


00:32:46.707 --> 00:32:48.299
Carlos, I don't understand.


00:32:48.587 --> 00:32:51.226
Why do you say
I'm acting strangely?


00:32:52.427 --> 00:32:55.066
That's what you told Julia
when you were alone, right?


00:32:55.267 --> 00:32:57.178
That I'm acting strangely.


00:32:57.627 --> 00:32:59.538
Isn't that what he said?


00:33:06.667 --> 00:33:08.259
Come here! Come here!


00:33:09.467 --> 00:33:10.866
Grab him, Julio!


00:33:12.267 --> 00:33:13.177
Julio!


00:33:13.547 --> 00:33:14.457
Julio!


00:33:25.667 --> 00:33:26.782
Grab him!


00:33:27.267 --> 00:33:28.336
Grab him!


00:33:28.507 --> 00:33:29.940
I've got him, I've got him!


00:33:33.387 --> 00:33:35.617
Carlos, Carlos!
Listen to me!


00:33:35.787 --> 00:33:37.584
Julia's cheating...


00:33:46.307 --> 00:33:49.458
Let's see what this bastard
has to say for himself.


00:33:49.627 --> 00:33:50.537
No!


00:33:51.707 --> 00:33:53.140
I'm scared!


00:34:13.667 --> 00:34:15.578
Isn't Julia kind of overreacting?


00:34:15.787 --> 00:34:16.936
About what?


00:34:17.067 --> 00:34:18.978
Not letting him talk and all that.


00:34:19.187 --> 00:34:21.747
What's he gonna do, hypnotize us?


00:34:22.427 --> 00:34:23.542
I don't know.


00:34:24.107 --> 00:34:28.100
We could ask him why they're here,
what the fuck they're doing here...


00:34:28.667 --> 00:34:31.056
That weird car Julia saw,
the one you drew...


00:34:31.227 --> 00:34:32.137
Yeah.


00:34:32.347 --> 00:34:34.907
Maybe he came in it
and he's got it parked somewhere.


00:34:35.067 --> 00:34:38.104
-Don't you wanna see it?
-Yeah, sure I do.


00:34:38.267 --> 00:34:41.065
If he could brainwash us
he'd have done it by now.


00:34:41.267 --> 00:34:43.019
Take off his gag.


00:35:03.907 --> 00:35:04.783
Wait.


00:35:06.107 --> 00:35:07.256
Come here.


00:35:16.867 --> 00:35:19.062
Maybe it is the real Angel.


00:35:20.107 --> 00:35:21.256
So?


00:35:21.987 --> 00:35:24.376
If it's Angel,
he's bound to go back


00:35:24.547 --> 00:35:28.062
and tell Julia I didn't listen to her
and let him talk.


00:35:28.427 --> 00:35:31.976
I'm not gonna let that bastard
give me away.


00:35:33.187 --> 00:35:36.702
Just untie his hands and feet
and let him go.


00:35:43.867 --> 00:35:46.461
Angel, if you are Angel...
I hope you understand,


00:35:46.667 --> 00:35:47.656
okay?


00:35:50.787 --> 00:35:52.266
I suggest you go


00:35:52.427 --> 00:35:54.338
to the shopping malls
to the north.


00:35:54.547 --> 00:35:56.981
There were no people around.
You know the way, right?


00:35:59.067 --> 00:36:00.659
If you're not Angel...


00:36:01.547 --> 00:36:02.059
Don't!


00:36:03.187 --> 00:36:06.782
Don't take off the gag!
Turn around and beat it!


00:36:08.667 --> 00:36:09.986
You got that?


00:36:32.907 --> 00:36:33.896
Hi.


00:36:40.067 --> 00:36:42.786
Isn't it Carlos' turn?
It's early.


00:36:43.227 --> 00:36:44.660
I couldn't sleep.


00:36:46.307 --> 00:36:47.217
Yeah.


00:36:59.907 --> 00:37:01.625
He took out the gun?


00:37:03.827 --> 00:37:05.579
You got that, motherfucker?


00:37:06.227 --> 00:37:06.977
Well?


00:37:13.267 --> 00:37:15.019
There are no bullets,
it's just in case.


00:37:15.707 --> 00:37:17.823
It's not even loaded.


00:37:17.987 --> 00:37:21.024
I got it from a sporting goods store
on my way over here.


00:37:21.667 --> 00:37:22.941
He showed it to you?


00:37:23.387 --> 00:37:26.060
No, I saw it in his pants.


00:37:26.267 --> 00:37:29.782
I guess he didn't want to worry me
by taking it out.


00:37:31.987 --> 00:37:33.215
I guess.


00:37:39.787 --> 00:37:42.017
This is the first thing
we should have done.


00:37:43.987 --> 00:37:46.182
I don't know why
I didn't think of it sooner.


00:37:46.507 --> 00:37:48.702
He's impressive.
He knows what he's doing.


00:37:51.507 --> 00:37:55.022
If he knew what he was doing
he'd have thrown you out as well.


00:37:57.267 --> 00:37:59.497
At least now we know
we got rid of that freak.


00:38:07.507 --> 00:38:09.384
Thanks for coming back.


00:38:38.867 --> 00:38:42.018
Those are pages
from a city guide, right?


00:38:42.707 --> 00:38:44.937
Yeah. It's the best view
of the city.


00:38:45.067 --> 00:38:48.457
But they're printed
on both sides.


00:38:48.667 --> 00:38:50.385
How did you manage that?


00:38:50.667 --> 00:38:52.942
I took two guides from taxis
on the way here.


00:38:53.067 --> 00:38:55.137
These are the quickest routes.


00:38:55.307 --> 00:38:58.856
We'll have to make runs.
Julio, this is your apartment?


00:38:59.027 --> 00:39:00.016
Yeah.


00:39:00.187 --> 00:39:02.417
You'll need us to pick up
your things.


00:39:02.867 --> 00:39:04.016
Yeah.


00:39:04.227 --> 00:39:05.660
What's this line?


00:39:05.867 --> 00:39:08.745
This is the area cut off
by the military.


00:39:08.947 --> 00:39:11.177
The whole area under the ship


00:39:11.347 --> 00:39:13.577
and these are the barricades
I mentioned.


00:39:13.787 --> 00:39:14.697
Okay.


00:39:14.907 --> 00:39:16.340
Right, first we'll go


00:39:16.507 --> 00:39:17.860
through here to pick up


00:39:18.027 --> 00:39:21.224
the generator for when the power
goes out, which it will.


00:39:21.667 --> 00:39:24.864
Then we'll look for
a bookstore downtown.


00:39:25.027 --> 00:39:28.064
We'll need manuals on
telecommunications, electronics,


00:39:28.947 --> 00:39:32.735
stuff like that.
I'm making a list on the laptop.


00:39:33.187 --> 00:39:35.621
Who goes with who?
Who stays home?


00:39:35.827 --> 00:39:38.136
Nobody.
If we go, it's all three of us.


00:39:38.307 --> 00:39:39.581
Why's that?


00:39:40.027 --> 00:39:42.700
If Angel wasn't Angel,
what happened to the real Angel?


00:39:42.907 --> 00:39:44.465
What if one of us gets left alone


00:39:44.667 --> 00:39:46.225
and they switch us?


00:39:46.387 --> 00:39:49.584
We stick together, no exceptions!


00:39:50.507 --> 00:39:51.496
Damn!


00:39:52.267 --> 00:39:53.256
What?


00:39:55.587 --> 00:39:57.976
I found a two euro coin!


00:40:07.227 --> 00:40:08.546
Are you sure?


00:40:08.747 --> 00:40:11.307
-There are some swings over there.
-Yeah.


00:40:11.467 --> 00:40:13.378
I wouldn't go near them.


00:40:13.587 --> 00:40:16.624
When I went by there
I saw some nasty-looking guys.


00:40:17.307 --> 00:40:18.899
Very dangerous.


00:40:19.787 --> 00:40:22.176
Seriously, with guns and everything.
They tried to shoot me.


00:40:22.347 --> 00:40:25.180
You couldn't pay me
to go over there.


00:40:25.907 --> 00:40:27.499
A gas station.


00:40:28.427 --> 00:40:30.987
With enough gasoline
we can make a bomb.


00:40:31.187 --> 00:40:33.064
-But Carlos...
-There are other ways.


00:40:33.267 --> 00:40:34.586
A bomb is a bit...


00:40:34.787 --> 00:40:37.142
I'm not talking about killing anyone.


00:40:37.307 --> 00:40:40.185
It's just in case
we need to scare someone.


00:40:40.827 --> 00:40:42.419
We're not that far from home.


00:40:42.587 --> 00:40:45.784
As long as we don't head that way
we're fine.


00:40:58.747 --> 00:41:00.658
The water's been cut off.


00:41:01.347 --> 00:41:03.258
-Already?
-Yeah.


00:41:04.427 --> 00:41:07.260
We'll have to get more bottles.
Should I wake Carlos up?


00:41:07.467 --> 00:41:10.345
No. Are there any more
in the kitchen?


00:41:10.547 --> 00:41:12.822
-Yeah, I'll get them.
-No, I'll go.


00:41:28.147 --> 00:41:31.025
When you walked by
in the towel earlier...


00:41:32.587 --> 00:41:34.145
I saw your ass.


00:41:34.787 --> 00:41:37.017
You did that on purpose, right?


00:41:37.827 --> 00:41:38.942
What?


00:41:39.187 --> 00:41:42.020
No way, you're joking.
How can you think that?


00:41:42.227 --> 00:41:45.424
Come on, you know exactly
when your ass is in view.


00:41:45.587 --> 00:41:47.464
Especially if there's a guy looking.


00:41:47.827 --> 00:41:50.660
Well, you're less careful
if he's already seen it.


00:41:50.867 --> 00:41:52.619
I've already seen it?


00:41:52.827 --> 00:41:55.136
I thought we agreed
we didn't have sex.


00:41:55.307 --> 00:41:58.185
We didn't, but you probably
saw my ass.


00:41:59.387 --> 00:42:00.456
Right.


00:42:03.507 --> 00:42:06.021
-Are you sure we didn't have sex?
-I don't know.


00:42:22.987 --> 00:42:25.217
Do you know how the generator works?


00:42:27.987 --> 00:42:30.217
It's still too dark.


00:42:31.027 --> 00:42:34.178
Wait until your eyes adjust.
You'll see more.


00:42:42.987 --> 00:42:46.024
That's it?
This is all we're gonna see?


00:42:46.907 --> 00:42:48.659
What else do you wanna see?


00:43:01.827 --> 00:43:03.704
Shit, the power's out.


00:43:04.067 --> 00:43:05.216
Julia?


00:43:05.467 --> 00:43:06.456
What?


00:43:06.667 --> 00:43:08.897
Lower your voice, you'll wake him.


00:43:09.027 --> 00:43:11.257
Are you still keeping watch?


00:43:11.427 --> 00:43:12.337
Yeah.


00:43:13.427 --> 00:43:15.702
Go back to bed.


00:43:20.307 --> 00:43:24.300
Get some rest.
I'll never get back to sleep anyway.


00:43:39.147 --> 00:43:41.581
Remind me when we go out tomorrow


00:43:41.787 --> 00:43:44.824
to get a 300-foot extension lead


00:43:45.347 --> 00:43:47.622
for the generator.
It's silent...


00:43:47.827 --> 00:43:50.057
but it's better off
in the stairwell.


00:43:50.427 --> 00:43:51.985
Or upstairs.


00:43:52.587 --> 00:43:55.181
We'll find one that's...


00:43:57.867 --> 00:43:59.141
Carlos, what...


00:44:04.107 --> 00:44:07.543
''Tune UHF... We're still here.''


00:44:07.747 --> 00:44:08.896
Damn!


00:44:12.027 --> 00:44:13.016
Carlos?


00:44:24.787 --> 00:44:26.345
I'm only asking you


00:44:26.507 --> 00:44:28.065
for one thing.


00:44:28.267 --> 00:44:31.304
When I ask you for the paper
don't take half an hour


00:44:31.467 --> 00:44:33.025
to bring it.


00:44:33.547 --> 00:44:35.424
Why don't you leave it
on the table?


00:44:35.667 --> 00:44:39.137
I've told you a thousand times
I don't want any papers on it.


00:44:39.787 --> 00:44:41.345
I can't be reading a piece of paper.


00:44:41.507 --> 00:44:43.816
This isn't the news, this is war.


00:44:45.267 --> 00:44:46.905
Then why keep asking for it?


00:44:47.067 --> 00:44:49.137
When we're on the air.


00:44:49.387 --> 00:44:51.264
I don't want it
when we're on the air.


00:44:51.467 --> 00:44:53.059
We are on the air.


00:44:54.107 --> 00:44:56.780
-We were, but you stopped.
-No.


00:44:56.987 --> 00:44:58.864
-You stopped.
-No, we're still on...


00:44:59.507 --> 00:45:02.260
This bozo claims to speak
for Madrid's refugees?


00:45:02.467 --> 00:45:04.617
-You stopped, right?
-No, damn it!


00:45:09.467 --> 00:45:12.539
More lights. We're not the only ones
with a generator.


00:45:12.747 --> 00:45:15.136
We're not the only ones
watching this.


00:45:16.867 --> 00:45:20.940
All those people listening to this guy
clueless to the danger we're all in...


00:45:21.067 --> 00:45:24.298
Carlos, there's no need to exaggerate.


00:45:24.587 --> 00:45:26.464
I'm being logical, Julio.


00:45:26.707 --> 00:45:29.346
If they went to the trouble
of trying to fool us,


00:45:29.507 --> 00:45:31.737
three schmucks in an apartment...


00:45:31.947 --> 00:45:35.462
won't they try to trick
these people on TV?


00:45:36.307 --> 00:45:38.218
I'm going to bed.


00:45:38.427 --> 00:45:40.987
Me too, my head's killing me.


00:45:43.267 --> 00:45:44.382
By the way,


00:45:44.547 --> 00:45:47.744
I'll leave the laptop on
so you can check out my notes.


00:45:47.947 --> 00:45:49.221
See you tomorrow.


00:45:49.427 --> 00:45:50.985
...imposed by the government


00:45:51.187 --> 00:45:53.064
due to this supposed threat.


00:45:53.267 --> 00:45:55.462
We're convinced there might be...


00:46:08.787 --> 00:46:09.902
Already?


00:46:10.547 --> 00:46:11.866
Sorry.


00:46:22.227 --> 00:46:24.502
-You know what we can do?
-What?


00:46:24.707 --> 00:46:26.299
With the cans and the hose...


00:46:26.467 --> 00:46:29.698
Since the heater isn't working,


00:46:29.987 --> 00:46:32.342
we can run the hose out the window,


00:46:32.507 --> 00:46:34.099
roll it up in a circle


00:46:35.587 --> 00:46:37.976
and the sun will heat the water.


00:46:38.187 --> 00:46:39.779
That would be nice.


00:46:41.827 --> 00:46:44.216
I think I can pull it off.


